<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan's BSPA group buys 54,000T U.S. soybeans.</title>
<headline>Taiwan's BSPA group buys 54,000T U.S. soybeans.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan's Breakfast Soybean Procurement Association's Kaohsiung division bought one 54,000-tonne shipment of U.S. soybeans at a retender on Wednesday from Cargill, traders said.  </p>
<p>The shipment was bought on a cost-and-freight basis, traders said.</p>
<p>The BSPA Kaohsiung division comprises Great Wall Enterprise, President Enterprises, Ttet Union and Tai Hwa Oil.</p>
<p>Details of the tender are as follows:</p>
<p> Type	Tonnes  Date/Location		 Price/Futures</p>
<p>			 U.S. Gulf   Pacific N.W.  104.96 UScents/May</p>
<p>Soybeans  54,000  March 16-30 April 1-15</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (5080815)</p>
